{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a58248a098943429","name":"Sith Talisman","source":{"id":"source:reference-a58248a098943429","title":"Sith Talisman","revision":20535,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:02:21Z","sha256":"f378e2a3e2aba281bf9e84eeeb41213c6dff276596331342700fc3a6438e1f54","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20535","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sith%20Talisman&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a58248a098943429","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Sith Talisman enhances its wearer's Force attacks. When Jedi first discover Sith Talismans, they find the trinkets can be made to serve the Light without adverse consequences. However, to counteract this exploitation, later Sith purposely infuse Sith Talismans with malignant energy, making them anathema to Jedi. The Jedi Council subsequently ban their use, and following ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Hyperspace War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Hyperspace_War?action=edit&redlink=1"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Shadows"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Shadows"}," willfully target the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Artifacts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Artifacts"}," for annihilation.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A bitter argument breaks out as Galactic Museum of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," curators fiercely assert the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Artifacts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Artifacts"},", like any historical curios, belong in a museum. Brokering a compromise, the Chancellor's office grants the museum rights to display ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Artifacts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Artifacts"},", except for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Holocrons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Holocrons"},", which are surrendered to the Jedi Temple.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The wearer of a Sith Talisman adds 1d6 to their damage with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Powers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Powers","referenceId":"reference:85acec94cd1ca5f3"},". They increase their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"}," by 1 when they first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. The wearer can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
